          "title": "Continuous Optimization for p-adic Models",
          "title_zh": "p 进模型的连续优化",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.25501v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_top",
          "organization": "DeepMind",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.25501",
          "summary": "The paper presents a method for native continuous gradient descent on machine learning models with p-adic parameters by working over the Berkovich affine line, a path-connected metric-tree expansion of the p-adic numbers that admits interpretable points and local derivatives. It formulates gradient descent plus momentum and Adam variants, shows linear models with p-adic coefficients can learn modular arithmetic, and demonstrates linear regression and classification on binary-encoded hierarchies.",
