          "title_zh": "SAM-V：面向多视图实例分割的几何感知分割一切模型",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.25490v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.25490",
          "summary": "The paper proposes SAM-V, which instead of post-hoc mask matching integrates features from the feed-forward geometry model VGGT directly into SAM and trains end-to-end for cross-view instance prediction, using prompt fusion with view-specific camera tokens and local geometry features plus a mask decoder attending to dense 2D and 3D features. On the IGGT 3D tracking benchmark it improves overall IoU by 5 points and frame-level recall by 12 points on the ScanNet++ split over the state-of-the-art multi-view instance segmentation baseline, and leads on all metrics on the zero-shot ScanNet split.",
