          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.25482",
          "summary": "The paper proposes Terminal Shrinkage Averaging, which interpolates between the raw final iterate and the average of recent checkpoints to balance late-training optimization progress against terminal variation, and analyzes how it changes the preferred terminal learning-rate schedule under a local quadratic approximation. Controlled NanoChat experiments show the schedule-estimator interaction, the gains transfer to depth-22 NanoChat, and a qualifying time-to-GPT-2 run finishes faster than the public baseline used in the experiments.",
